From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoCo starter <coco-starter@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:58:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] null: render frames and save one after a checkpoint

The null UI normally discards every scanline. Attach XRoar's own
software renderer to it instead, rendering into a memory buffer, so the
machine's SAM/VDG (or GIME) output and palette are rendered exactly as
for a window.

When coco_video_checkpoint() is called, the second frame completed
afterwards is written as a binary PPM to the path in the COCO_VIDEO
environment variable, and a COCO_VIDEO,<tick>,<width>,<height> line is
logged on stderr. The first frame completed after the checkpoint was
partly scanned before it, so it is skipped.

Without COCO_VIDEO nothing is written; the renderer still runs.

This is test equipment for the CoCo starter's scripts/coco.py.
